<title>USA: CompuServe rescinds earnings remarks.</title>
<headline>CompuServe rescinds earnings remarks.</headline>
<dateline>COLUMBUS, Ohio 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>CompuServe Corp Friday said it rescinded earnings remarks made earlier in the day, saying that while it seeks to return to profitability &quot;as soon as possible,&quot; it is not projecting results beyond the second quarter.</p>
<p>The company had announced that it expects a second-quarter loss of about $0.10 to $0.15 per share.  </p>
<p>At a morning news conference in Munich the company's president of international operations, Steven Stanbrook, had said the company would turn profits in the third and fourth quarters.</p>
<p>The company responded with a statement saying that it isn't projecting when it would return to profitability.</p>
</text>
